RFC 6902 not built-in, but jq can build patches: `[{op: "replace", path: "/name", value: "new"}]`. Apply patch operations: ```jq
reduce .[] as $op (.; 
  if $op.op == "replace" then setpath($op.path | split("/") | .[1:]; $op.value) 
  elif $op.op == "remove" then delpaths([$op.path | split("/") | .[1:]]) 
  else . end)
```. For real JSON Patch: external tools like `json-patch`.

